  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para><figure><media alt="A graph. "><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1903c3abc2af4c6a8ec0ea2c81f2b371a971b2b3"/></media></figure></para>
<para> The graph above shows the population of a city from 1900 to 2000. Use the graph to answer questions 1 - 5.</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the average rate of change of the population between 1930 and 1950? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers: </para>
    <para>About 250 people per year. The population was 40,000 in 1930 and about 45,000 in 1950, an increase of 5,000 people over 20 years, which equals 250 people per year.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="18f95d76-2cf0-4155-b372-743962080f9a" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="a1675ebf-57d7-458b-b883-2c2253f7debe" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="positive" data-solution-options="[&quot;positive&quot;, &quot;negative&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Decide if the average rate of change is positive or negative for the time period from 1930 to 1940.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The correct answer is: positive.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="86593013-6bb2-4b6c-b285-5c2d26f37ba4" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="negative" data-solution-options="[&quot;positive&quot;, &quot;negative&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Decide if the average rate of change is positive or negative for the time period from 1950 to 1970.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The correct answer is: negative.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="f5929df6-160f-4721-a943-5da6064a7541" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="negative" data-solution-options="[&quot;positive&quot;, &quot;negative&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Decide if the average rate of change is positive or negative for the time period from 1930 to 1970.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The correct answer is: negative.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
